---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---
<Layout title="About Brian Knight | Broker Pal" description="Meet Brian Knight, founder of Broker Pal, and learn about his more than 26 years of experience across the mortgage industry.">
<div class="page">
  <div class="kicker">MEET THE FOUNDER</div>
  <h1>A lending perspective shaped by experience.</h1>
  <p class="intro">I'm Brian Knight, founder of Broker Pal, LLC. My career in the mortgage industry began in July 2000 in Bozeman, Montana. More than 26 years later, the experience I've gained across the lending process continues to shape how I approach investment-property financing.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>How it started</h2>
    <p>My introduction to the mortgage business came through my father, Steve Knight, who owned a mortgage company in the Lilburn, Georgia area during the 1990s. After my family moved west, my dad started a mortgage business in Montana and invited me to learn the trade. I was ready for a direction, and I said yes.</p>
    <p>He started by teaching me the fundamentals as a loan processor. One lesson stayed with me: to understand a loan, you need to understand every part of the process. That foundation shaped the way I approached each role that followed.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience across the lending process</h2>
    <p>Over the course of my career, I've worked in processing support management, compliance, credit-risk support, quality control, auditing, due-diligence underwriting, and mortgage brokerage. I was previously a licensed mortgage broker through Knight Financial.</p>
    <p>Those different perspectives taught me to look beyond a single rate or loan request—to understand the documentation, risk, property, people, and details that all contribute to a financing decision.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why I created Broker Pal</h2>
    <p>Broker Pal was created to make investment-property financing conversations more approachable, organized, and useful. Real estate investors deserve clear communication and a thoughtful discussion of the property and the plan behind it.</p>
    <p>Whether you're exploring a rental purchase, refinancing an investment property, or considering another business-purpose financing option, the first step should be understanding what you're trying to accomplish and what information is available.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <h2>A straightforward place to start.</h2>
    <p>Tell us about the investment property or financing goal you're considering. We'll take the time to understand the request and explain the next steps.</p>
    <a href="/contact">Start a conversation →</a>
  </section>
</div>
</Layout>
<style>
